# STRICT RULE: Sanity CMS Scope

**Exactly TWO Sanity document types exist. Nothing else.**

Do NOT create additional Sanity document types without human approval.

## Allowed Document Types

### 1. Article Document

```typescript
// schemas/article.ts
import { defineField, defineType } from 'sanity'

export default defineType({
  name: 'article',
  title: 'Artikel',
  type: 'document',
  fields: [
    defineField({ name: 'title_id', title: 'Judul (ID)', type: 'string', validation: (r) => r.required() }),
    defineField({ name: 'title_en', title: 'Title (EN)', type: 'string' }),
    defineField({ name: 'slug', title: 'Slug', type: 'slug', options: { source: 'title_id' }, validation: (r) => r.required() }),
    defineField({ 
      name: 'coverImage', 
      title: 'Cover Image', 
      type: 'image',
      options: { hotspot: true },
      fields: [{ name: 'alt', type: 'string', title: 'Alt Text' }],
      validation: (r) => r.required()
    }),
    defineField({ name: 'category', title: 'Kategori', type: 'reference', to: [{ type: 'category' }], validation: (r) => r.required() }),
    defineField({ name: 'excerpt_id', title: 'Ringkasan (ID)', type: 'text', rows: 3, validation: (r) => r.required().max(200) }),
    defineField({ name: 'excerpt_en', title: 'Excerpt (EN)', type: 'text', rows: 3, validation: (r) => r.max(200) }),
    defineField({ name: 'body_id', title: 'Isi (ID)', type: 'portableText', validation: (r) => r.required() }),
    defineField({ name: 'body_en', title: 'Body (EN)', type: 'portableText' }),
    defineField({ name: 'publishedAt', title: 'Tanggal Publikasi', type: 'datetime', initialValue: () => new Date().toISOString() }),
    defineField({ name: 'authorName', title: 'Nama Penulis', type: 'string', validation: (r) => r.required() }),
  ],
})
```

### 2. Category Document

```typescript
// schemas/category.ts
import { defineField, defineType } from 'sanity'

export default defineType({
  name: 'category',
  title: 'Kategori',
  type: 'document',
  fields: [
    defineField({ name: 'title_id', title: 'Nama (ID)', type: 'string', validation: (r) => r.required() }),
    defineField({ name: 'title_en', title: 'Name (EN)', type: 'string', validation: (r) => r.required() }),
    defineField({ name: 'slug', title: 'Slug', type: 'slug', options: { source: 'title_id' }, validation: (r) => r.required() }),
  ],
})
```

## Villager Permission Boundary

| Action | Allowed |
|--------|---------|
| Create/edit/publish `article` | ✅ Yes |
| Select existing `category` | ✅ Yes |
| Create new `category` | ✅ Yes (keep simple) |
| Edit homestays | ❌ NO (hardcoded) |
| Edit attractions | ❌ NO (hardcoded) |
| Edit booklet | ❌ NO (hardcoded) |
| Edit downloads | ❌ NO (hardcoded) |
| Edit site settings | ❌ NO (doesn't exist) |
| Edit page structure | ❌ NO (code only) |

## What Does NOT Go in Sanity

These are **hardcoded in the repository** as TypeScript data files:

- `data/homestays.ts` - Homestay listings
- `data/attractions.ts` - Tourist attractions
- `data/booklet.ts` - Flora & fauna booklet pages
- `data/downloads.ts` - After-movie URL + guidebook metadata
